    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d841">

                <pb facs="0899" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg811"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum handed to Mr. Adee March 1, 1904, by
                        Minister Grip.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Sweden and Norway at Washington</hi></placeName>.
                            [<date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1904-03-01"
                    >undated</date>].</dateline></opener>
                <p>Messrs. Kelly &amp; Co., of New York, charterers of the Norwegian steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Farmand</hi>, have informed this legation that the
                    steamer has been prohibited by the Santo Domingo authorities from entering the
                    harbor of Macoris and there loading a cargo.</p>
                <pb facs="0900" n="812" xml:id="pg812"/>
                <p>The legation would feel highly gratified if the United States man-of-war
                    stationed near said port might be instructed to assist the Norwegian
                    steamer.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
